## Interview Takeaway

The key insight is recognizing that the input array is already the **level-order traversal of a complete binary tree**. Since each level in a complete binary tree contains `1, 2, 4, 8, ...` nodes, you can process the array directly in chunks of those sizes, sort each chunk, and avoid building or traversing the tree entirely. This makes the solution cleaner while maintaining the required `O(n log n)` time complexity.
